  "promptSpec": {
    "id": "walker-gear",
    "generator": "OpenAI imagegen built-in",
    "prompt": "Use case stylized-concept. Original fan-made detailed pixel-art game sprite sheet faithfully depicting the standard ENEMY WALKER GEAR from Metal Gear Solid V The Phantom Pain, based on Yoji Shinkawa official Walker Gear concept art. Compact man-height biped weapons platform, military olive-gray polygonal open-rear cockpit/body, large faceted slanted forward armor shield forming an angular box, small wedge-shaped sensor on a short top stalk (NOT humanoid head), one thin two-link mechanical manipulator ending in a gripper, two prominent angular mechanical legs with round knee joints and exposed pistons, small flat wide feet, tiny heel wheels. Mounted compact machinegun on body flank. NO human rider so reusable empty vehicle asset; not D-Walker's small camera mast design, no giant mech, no four legs, no glowing face or eyes, no Gundam wings. Entire silhouette resembles angular walking chair / armored platform, not a barrel-bodied battle droid. Orthographic SIDE profile facingRIGHT, consistent scale, crisp pixel clusters. EXACT4columns×4rows16 authored poses on flatpure#FF00FFmagenta background, thin purecyan boundarygrid. Entire machine inside CENTRAL60% cell with20% clear margins; identical grounded scale. Row1 four sensor scanning/idle articulation phases. Row2 four genuinely alternate mechanical walking gaits, large circular knee joints visibly flexing. Row3 aiming, firing compactmachinegun with small yellowflash, recoil, recover. Row4 hit tilt, legbrace crouch, recovery, idle. No labels, text, numbers, logos, UI, scenery or ground shadows; all limbs and weapon muzzle inside eachcell, no cropped parts or repeated translated poses.",
    "referenceUrls": [
      "https://www.creativeuncut.com/gallery-27/mgs5-walker-gear.html",
      "https://us-support.konami.com/hc/en-us/articles/4633552454807-Controls-On-Walker-Gear"
    ],
    "review": "Official concept silhouette visually inspected via its mirror. Retains faceted open-rear platform, short sensor, mechanical knees, feet and gripper. Original fan-made pixel adaptation, not a 1:1 reproduction claim."
  },
